==== stdout ====
Usage: raphael unfavorite <path> [options]
       raphael unfavorite --id <id> [options]

Remove an area or project from favorites.

An item that is not a favorite succeeds without a change, and so does an id that
names nothing.

Options:
      --id <id>
          Address by stable id instead of path.
      --json
          Print the result as one JSON document.
  -h, --help
          Show help.

Examples:
  raphael unfavorite /work
  raphael unfavorite --id 42
  raphael unfavorite /work/raphael --json

Prints:
  The item with its path and favorite state; Unchanged when it already was in
  that state, and a plain sentence when the id names nothing. JSON carries
  `nodeId`, `isFavorite`, `changed` and `node`.

Next: raphael favorites

See also: raphael help favorite
